LaunchAgain
===========

Third-party code
----------------

None. This project has zero external dependencies. Every line that ships is in this
repository, and the Swift package declares no package dependencies of any kind — check
Package.swift.

Everything else it uses comes from the operating system:

  * Swift standard library, Foundation, AppKit, SwiftUI, Core Graphics, Core Services
    — Apple Inc., included with macOS and Xcode.
  * The command line tools it invokes, all shipped with macOS and all called with
    absolute paths and argument arrays:
        /usr/bin/codesign      re-signing and verifying generated bundles
        /usr/bin/iconutil      assembling .icns files from a generated iconset
        /bin/cp                APFS copy-on-write cloning (cp -Rpc)
        /usr/bin/lipo          reading a binary's architectures
        /usr/bin/xattr         removing com.apple.quarantine from a bundle we created
        /usr/sbin/spctl        recording the Gatekeeper assessment for diagnostics
        /usr/bin/open          opening GUI applications and local documentation
        /usr/bin/du            measuring allocated disk usage
        /bin/ps                reading process arguments for diagnostics
        /usr/bin/hdiutil       building the release disk image
        .../LaunchServices.framework/.../Support/lsregister
                               registering a generated bundle, used only as a fallback
                               when the public LSRegisterURL call is unavailable

Applications you point it at
----------------------------

This program creates copies of applications you already have installed, on your own
machine, for your own use. It does not redistribute anyone's software, and it does not
bundle, embed or ship any third-party application.

A copy created this way is modified in three ways — a rewritten bundle identifier and
display name, a generated icon, and a small launcher shim — and is re-signed ad-hoc by
your Mac. It is therefore no longer signed by the original developer, and it is not
represented as being so: every generated bundle carries `MALGeneratedBy` and
`MALOriginalBundleIdentifier` in its Info.plist.

The original application is never modified, moved, re-signed or redistributed.

